module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.declared_uncitedness_ignored_by_admission

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef }

data declared_uncitedness_ignored_by_admission: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "declared_uncitedness_ignored_by_admission" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a rate table carries CitedFigureStanding but its consumer admits any matching row without reading that standing. HARM: a declared TranscribedUncited figure becomes an admitted hardware operating rate. SPECIMEN: gunbc#10954 product.node_power_envelope rank_specific_2dpc_clock refused empty rows but admitted nonempty uncited rows; the positive witness itself supplied such a table. DISTINGUISHING FACT: row presence and provenance are independent inputs; refusing absence does not refuse explicitly uncited presence. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, caught during review. REPAIR: the matching-row arm consumes table.evidence and propagates RankSpecificRateUncited with its read obligation through ChannelClockUnresolved and MemoryBandwidthUnresolved. The absent-row arm remains RankSpecificRateMissing. CONTROLS: test.claim.node_power_envelope_witness emptying_rank_specific_ceiling_rows_does_not_admit_an_effective_rate and uncited_rank_specific_rows_do_not_admit_an_effective_rate, paired with a_rank_specific_ceiling_row_admits_the_capped_effective_rate. CEILING: mechanically preventable for consuming the declared provenance, with citation truth remaining an external boundary. NEXT TRIGGER: acceptance derives and enforces provenance consumption for every admitted figure, rather than relying on each domain's match and witnesses. A CitedToAuthority constructor does not independently prove that its document attests the figure; the synthetic positive fixture cites itself and establishes no Ampere operating rate.",

    "FOUND AGAIN, 2026-11-21, one domain over and in a decision that spends money: the hardware model's rows were consumed as complete in an accelerator purchase comparison while their OWN standing said otherwise. extdeps.gpu.gigabyte::gigabyte_r9700_ai_top_figures_standing is TranscribedUncited -- a transcription with no authority attached -- and the R9700 and Gigabyte figures still entered the comparison; extdeps.gpu.nvidia::nvidia_rtx_2000_ada_catalog declares no memory_bandwidth at all, which did not stop the row being used where bandwidth is exactly what decides; and the H11SSL unit-1 intake receipt (gunbc.machine_intake.supermicro_h11ssl_unit1_hand_install_receipt, the host now named dan) carries accounts_and_ssh_keys_report as NotRelayed while that host's access was gated by a key sitting outside gunbc.compute.remote_build's fleet_authorized_keys roster. Three different declarations of incompleteness -- uncited transcription, an absent field, an unrelayed report -- and one consumer behavior: none of them was read before the row was used.",

    "CHECKED, 2026-11-23, against the tree rather than the relay, because the receipt above asserts a consumption this lane could not find and a ledger row must not carry a path that does not exist. Three findings, each read at the declaration. (1) The purchase comparison the relay named does not read these rows: gunbc.gpu_market.catalog_boards builds its census from the NVIDIA catalogs alone (gpu_catalog_board_admissions lists no AMD or Gigabyte board), so the R9700 and Gigabyte figures never enter it. What those rows genuinely feed is installed-hardware identity -- gunbc.fleet.fleet_physical_inventory binds host-6ce85c gpu_board_02 and gpu_board_03 to them, which is where a 32 GiB capacity and a 300 W ceiling reach decisions about a running host with no mark on them. The cost the relay paid stands; the path is the inventory, not a cart. (2) The two absent-field specimens are typed where they are read: the h11 intake record answers its NotRelayed report as absence at the field accessor, so a consumer cannot read the unrelayed report as a value, and gunbc.gpu_market carries bandwidth as an optional figure rather than a zero, so nothing multiplies the RTX 2000 Ada missing bandwidth today -- the RTX 2000 Ada is in that census, which is why the typed absence is the thing that holds. What is owed there is not the absence but the decision that never consults the record: the access gate and the roster of keys still do not read it. (3) The admission accessor this class turns on, extdeps.gpu.types gpu_board_admission_facts, still answers an admission with bare facts and is called only by witnesses. gunbc.fleet.gpu_declared_figures_standing::gpu_admitted_board_figures is now the way in that hands the facts over with the standing the declaring module stated, or with the basis for having none; its consumer is the roster-admission item on this same plan, node 'fleet-truth-rosters-consume-the-read' of program 'fleet-truth-follows-the-machine', which is the trigger that turns it from a frontier into a guard. NEXT TRIGGER for this row stays as written, and NO instance is closed by this change: the module above is a declared frontier whose consumer is that roster item, and until it lands the only caller of gpu_board_power_ceiling_with_standing, gpu_catalog_memory_with_standing and gpu_admitted_board_figures is their own witness -- git grep finds no import of gunbc.fleet.gpu_declared_figures_standing in gunbc.fleet.fleet_physical_inventory or anywhere else in production. So the rung this row reports stays where it was, at mitigatable-caught-in-review: what the change establishes is that a standing can travel with the figure it qualifies and that an unmarked row now has to say its basis, which is the precondition the trigger needs, not the trigger met. Claiming the instance closed would be the reader-as-defect failure this very row names.",
    "WHAT THIS ADDS TO THE RECOGNITION RULE, stated so the row stays one row rather than three: the standing of a figure is an INPUT to the decision, not metadata beside it. Before a row enters a comparison, a rate table or an access decision, the consumer reads its standing -- TranscribedUncited, NotRelayed, an absent field -- and the conclusion carries that standing in its own text rather than dropping it at the boundary. The hardware case is the proof that the rule cannot live in each domain's match arm: the rate-table consumer was fixed to refuse uncited rows, and a year of hardware comparisons downstream of it still consumed the same rows as complete.",  ],
    "CHECKED, 2026-11-27, at the two consumer sites the 2026-11-21 receipt named, on node fleet-truth-declared-incompleteness-refuses-use (rn_AYHH104UYXBSJUVP94BE4X03S2). (1) THE COMPARISON SITE NOW READS THE STANDING BEFORE IT DECIDES: gunbc.gpu_market.comparison_standing::board_comparison_admission is the gate and the deciding fold gunbc.gpu_market.realization_join::realization_check_board calls it FIRST, answering a typed ComparisonStandingRefused that carries the standing value and the declaring module own read obligation, so a TranscribedUncited figure can no longer reach a capacity or ceiling verdict unread -- the same answer the rate table already gives at product.node_power_envelope::rank_specific_2dpc_clock, and no second provenance model. Blast radius, measured over all 47 GpuBoardCatalogFacts rows under dag/extdeps/gpu/: 4 newly refused (extdeps.gpu.amd::amd_radeon_ai_pro_r9700_board_facts and extdeps.gpu.gigabyte::gigabyte_r9700_ai_top_32g_board_facts, both figures marked; extdeps.gpu.nvidia::nvidia_rtx_5090_board_facts, both figures stated with no citation and no declared standing; nvidia_rtx_pro_6000_max_q_board_facts, memory marked), 5 admitted with an absent ceiling CARRIED visibly in ComparisonAdmitted.absent rather than refused and rather than read as a zero, 38 unremarked; no claim today joins any of the 4, which is why the gate is measured against the whole catalog rather than against the census (gunbc.gpu_market.catalog_boards carries NVIDIA rows only: amd hits 0, nvidia hits 49). (2) THE ACCESS SITE HAS A STANDING-CARRYING FOLD AND STILL NO GATE THAT READS IT, recorded as such rather than claimed closed: the row own 2026-11-23 paragraph says a claim of closure at this site is the reader-as-defect failure this row tracks. gunbc.host.host_authorized_keys_reconcile::host_access_admission refuses a key outside the roster with the accounts standing named, distinguishes refused-against-a-relayed-report from undecidable-on-an-undeclared-one by cause, downgrades a complete roster when the intake report declares itself incomplete, and admits only where that report is relayed AND cited to an authority -- carrying no obligation in that arm. But git grep finds its caller only in its own witness, so the access gate and the roster of keys still do not read it. THE NAMED CONSUMER AND ITS TRIGGER: the apply projection of the host-administrator account authorized_keys plan -- the first fold that turns a MembershipPlan from host_authorized_keys_reconcile into writes, the apply grain that module own comment reserves to a human at membership_effects_wholesale_refuse_policy_note -- must call host_access_admission and carry its accounts_keys arm into the receipt it writes, the way realization_join now calls board_comparison_admission. Until that fold exists the rung this row reports stays where the 2026-11-23 paragraph left it, at mitigatable-caught-in-review, and NO instance is closed by this change."
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.gpu.gigabyte", decl_name: "gigabyte_r9700_ai_top_figures_standing", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.gpu_market.catalog_boards", decl_name: "gpu_catalog_board_admissions", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_physical_inventory", decl_name: "gpu_board_02_asset", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.supermicro_h11ssl_unit1_hand_install_receipt", decl_name: "supermicro_h11ssl_unit1_hand_install", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.gpu.types", decl_name: "gpu_board_admission_facts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fleet.gpu_declared_figures_standing", decl_name: "gpu_admitted_board_figures", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.gpu.nvidia", decl_name: "nvidia_rtx_2000_ada_catalog", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.gpu_market.comparison_standing", decl_name: "board_comparison_admission", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.gpu_market.realization_join", decl_name: "realization_check_board", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.host.host_authorized_keys_reconcile", decl_name: "host_access_admission", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
